        "url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/neptune-analytics/latest/userguide/neptune-analytics-vs-neptune-database.html",
        "source": "aws-neptune-docs",
        "aws::graph::propositions": [
            "Neptune Analytics Knowledge Graph",
            "Neptune Analytics is a solution for quickly analyzing existing graph databases or graph datasets stored in a data lake.",
            "Neptune Analytics uses popular graph analytic algorithms and low-latency analytic queries.",
            "Neptune Analytics can be used to analyze and query graphs in data science workflows that build targeted content recommendations, assist with fraud investigations, and detect network threats.",
            "Neptune Analytics provides a simple API for loading, querying, and analyzing graph data, which removes the overhead of building and managing complex data-analytics pipelines.",
            "Neptune Analytics makes it easy to apply powerful algorithms both to the data in your Neptune Database and to graph data that's stored externally.",
            "Neptune Analytics can load a large dataset very quickly into memory, enabling the analysis of graphs with tens of billions of relationships and the processing of thousands of analytic queries per second using popular graph analytics algorithms."
        ],
